I'll read the current files before applying the patches.## 1. Review & Understand the Task

Apply the three patches proposed in the previous turn, plus the regression cases:

- **`src/utils/markdownParser.js`** — make `</file_change>` detection fence-aware (closers only count at depth 0), stop trimming the tag matchers (so indented examples are not envelopes), and make `isInsideCodeFence` aware of fenced envelope examples.
- **`src/utils/codeBlockExtractor.js`** — reuse the shared helpers, drop the `lines[i] !== '```'` legacy loop (breaks on trailing spaces, `\r`, ```` ```` ````, `~~~`).
- **`src/components/document/DocumentSummary.vue`** — same treatment instead of `line === '```'`.
- **`tests/fileChangeParser.test.mjs`** — standalone `node` script pinning the four failure cases (no test runner is installed, so it must be dependency-free).

## 2. Changes Summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/utils/markdownParser.js` | Add `isFenceClosedLater()`; rewrite the closer scan in `parseFileChangeBlock()` with a fence stack; tolerante tag matchers (0–3 leading spaces, no `.trim()`); fence-aware envelope handling in `isInsideCodeFence()`. |
| `src/utils/codeBlockExtractor.js` | Import `getFence`/`isClosingFence`/`getFileChangeOpenTag`/`parseFileChangeBlock` from `markdownParser`; delete duplicated envelope helpers; collect legacy bodies until a *valid* closing fence. |
| `src/components/document/DocumentSummary.vue` | Replace the depth counter + `line === '```'` with a fence stack and `parser.isClosingFence()`; envelope bodies consumed via `parser.parseFileChangeBlock()`. |
| `tests/fileChangeParser.test.mjs` | New, dependency-free regression script (`node tests/fileChangeParser.test.mjs`). |

## 3. The Changes

