## 4. Notes

- **Counter semantics:** `depth` starts at 1 for the envelope being parsed, `++` on an unfenced `<file_change …>`, `--` on a closing marker, block ends at `0`. Nested envelopes are written verbatim into the outer file (`parseBlocks` already jumps to `endIndex`), so extracted code blocks stay one-per-outer-envelope.
- **Fences mask tags:** inside a fence the tag lines are examples and never touch `depth`, which keeps an unbalanced sample from desynchronising the count.
- **Safety valve:** if the body never balances (a bare open-tag example), the block ends at the last closing marker seen instead of running to EOF.
- **`isInsideCodeFence()`** now skips complete envelopes via `parseFileChangeBlock()`; the `inFileChange` boolean and its private fence stack are gone, so nested-envelope handling has a single source of truth.
- **`isFenceClosedLater()` removed** — no longer referenced by any module or component in this workspace (the counter replaces it); its export was dropped as well.
