I'll review the current parsing logic on disk before changing anything.## 1. Review & Understand the Task

The current `<file_change>` / fence scanner still lets fences interfere with block boundaries, which is what produces the "the block ends three lines after a ```" symptom. Per your rules I will make the state machine **typed and counted, never flagged**:

- **Inside a `<file_change>` block: every other fence is content.** No ```` ``` ```` / `~~~` line can open, close, mask or shift anything. Only `<file_change …>` (`+1`) and `<file_change/>` / `</file_change>` (`−1`) move the counter; the block ends when it returns to `0`.
- **Inside a fenced block: only fences of that block's own delimiter count.** Opening fences of the same char `+1`, a closing fence of the same char (length ≥ innermost open) `−1`; when the counter reaches `0` the block ends. `~~~` inside a ```` ``` ```` block, another delimiter, or a `<file_change>` tag is content.
- **No flags anywhere**: `inCodeBlock`, `inFileChange`, `nestDepth`, `fenceStack` booleans/stacks replaced by `createFenceTracker()` + `trackFence()` counters shared by `parseBlocks`, `parseFileChangeBlock`, `isInsideCodeFence`, `codeBlockExtractor` and `DocumentSummary`.

## 2. Changes Summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/utils/markdownParser.js` | New shared `getFenceType()` / `createFenceTracker()` / `trackFence()` counter API. `parseFileChangeBlock()` counts tags only (fences ignored). `parseBlocks()` rewritten with the tracker. `isInsideCodeFence()` rewritten with the tracker. |
| `src/utils/codeBlockExtractor.js` | Legacy fence branch uses the shared tracker instead of `isClosingFence`/string compare. |
| `src/components/document/DocumentSummary.vue` | Uses the shared tracker instead of its private fence stack. |
| `tests/fileChangeParser.test.mjs` | New cases 10–14 pinning the reported failures and the counter rules. |

## 3. The Changes

